WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.330
These creek readings look dramatic.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.510
One blue bar seems twice as tall as the other.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.550
Before deciding that the water is twice as deep,

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.670
read the number at the bottom of the scale.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.850
The axis starts at thirty centimetres.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.860
The water was thirty six centimetres deep on Monday and

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.210
forty two on Tuesday.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.350
The rise is six centimetres.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.220
Restoring the missing thirty shows why twice the visible

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.230
height is only seven sixths of the original depth.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.390
Two tanks are shown on a second chart.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.380
The bottom line means twelve litres.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.760
Every interval adds two litres.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.870
One bar rises three intervals and the other rises seven.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.790
What is the ratio of the fuller tank to the other?

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:49.290
Three intervals add six litres, so the smaller

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.580
tank contains eighteen.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:54.550
Seven intervals add fourteen litres, so the larger one

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:55.480
contains twenty six.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:59.660
Twenty six to eighteen simplifies to thirteen to nine.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:02.640
Seven to three compares the visible pieces alone.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.480
The bottom label has rubbed off a chart.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:08.700
The values at the tops are thirty six and forty eight.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.210
The longer bar looks exactly three times as tall as

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.040
the shorter bar.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:15.100
What number was on the bottom line?

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.490
Imagine sliding the short bar beside the long one.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.450
Their tops are twelve units apart.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.980
That gap is two short bars, because the long bar

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:28.250
contains three of them.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.270
Each short bar therefore represents six units.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.170
The shorter bar ends at thirty six.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.990
Step down six and the erased label must be thirty.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:39.450
Check the long bar.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.860
Forty eight minus thirty gives eighteen,

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:44.230
which is exactly three times six.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.960
Cropping the same amount from two bars preserves the

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.150
difference between their tops.

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.410
A ratio uses the whole readings.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.180
On an unfamiliar chart, write the baseline and tick

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.710
interval before trusting what your eye sees.
